  -> K1 DOES NOT FIRE: the baseline loses on best pair separation 0.5x vs the CA's 2.4x. The CA-derived features carry something the static two-token conditional does not, so H3 survives its first real test and Gate 2 is licensed. This does NOT establish that the dynamics are necessary -- only that the cheapest deflation tried so far does not reproduce them. Baseline features cohering within families at p<0.05: fixed_point_fraction, cond_top1_mean, cond_entropy_mean (Gate 0's CA attractor share was 0.218, p~3e-4). Coherence is necessary for a fingerprint and is not by itself identification -- Gate 0's own lesson, where a coherent feature still gave 4/14 attribution. Exploratory-to-registered boundary: the COMPARISON is pre-registered in prereg.json and K1's rule was frozen before any of these numbers existed; the numbers themselves are new. Family is the independent unit throughout, so the six Pythia sizes are one observation.

